    {
      "claim": "L5 C139 shows that hPepT1 substrates such as lisinopril have low predicted passive diffusion but significantly higher in vivo human jejunal effective permeability because of carrier-mediated uptake; the query shares lisinopril's lysine primary-amine and zwitterionic diacid motif, supporting active transport as a route to F ≥ 20% despite poor passive permeability.",
      "card_ids": ["C139"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 C111 and C91 provide affirmative human absorption evidence for lisinopril (~25% absorption) and high solubility; L5 C172 and L1 ampicillin records (C08/C15/C19/C11) show that transporter/efflux substrates can still reach 29–43% oral bioavailability.",
      "card_ids": ["C111", "C91", "C172", "C08", "C15", "C19", "C11"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 C192/C221 and C219/C235 show low intrinsic hepatic clearance for related ACE inhibitors (enalapril, temocapril) in liver S9 fractions, suggesting hepatic first-pass loss is unlikely to be the dominant barrier if the query is absorbed; transferability is limited because these are ester prodrugs measured in rat/dog S9.",
      "card_ids": ["C192", "C221", "C219", "C235"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 high-clearance records for imipramine and mianserin (C204, C210, C229) are structurally unrelated to the query and do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C204", "C210", "C229"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C192", "C219", "C221", "C235"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No direct PEPT1 or other active-transport assay has been run on the query itself; lisinopril and related amino-acid/peptide-mimetic drugs are structural analogs.",
    "No direct hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability measurement exists for the query; L6 records are for related ACE inhibitor ester prodrugs in non-human S9 fractions.",
    "The benzazepinone scaffold may alter transporter recognition and metabolic fate relative to lisinopril.",
    "The estimated logD of -8.18 is a physicochemical prior and may overstate polarity relative to experimental zwitterionic ACE-inhibitor behavior."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F ≥ 20%) maintained. L5 hPepT1 evidence and lisinopril/ampicillin records provide affirmative absorption support despite poor passive permeability; L6 adds only low-transferability hepatic-clearance data for related ACE inhibitors showing low intrinsic clearance, which does not introduce affirmative F < 20% evidence. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query-specific ADME or oral F data are available."
}

